-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Modifications relative to upstream
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  - Compressed the per-group mandatory-read list (upstream ~39.4K tok -> lite
    8.8-9.3K tok, about -77%). The read list is documented in
    reference/prompts-lite.md; the lite reading set is described in SKILL.md.
  - Added two zero-image machine gates that upstream does not ship:
      * template/scripts/zorder_audit.py  (layer-order / occlusion auditor)
      * template/scripts/lite_gate.py     (single-command 4-axis gate)
  - Added three hard rules to the build contract
    (reference/build-contract-lite.md sections 12-14): enter-order = draw-order;
    coordinates must be literals; delivery must report ink-box / max-overlap /
    Z1-Z2 findings into BUILD_NOTES.
  - Added lite-specific reference docs: build-contract-lite.md, qc-lite.md,
    prompts-lite.md, lessons-lite.md, ENGINE.md.
  - Bundled copies of the upstream engine (template/), upstream example assets
    (examples/) and additional upstream reference docs (style-guide.md,
    motion-vocabulary.md, composition-and-light.md, narration-storyboard.md,
    research-brief.md, common-api.md, prompts.md, lessons.md) so that this
    package is self-contained and installable on its own.
  - Rewrote the bootstrap entry point (scripts/lite_bootstrap.py).
  - Renamed the upstream README files to UPSTREAM_README.md /
    UPSTREAM_README_zh.md (archived verbatim, with a note at the top saying they
    describe the full tier); this package's own README is README.md (English)
    plus README_zh.md (Simplified Chinese).
  - Replaced hard-coded, machine-specific absolute paths (Python / Node / ffmpeg
    locations) in the ported scripts with environment-variable overrides and
    generic fallbacks (A2E_PYTHON / A2E_NODE / A2E_FFMPEG, then PATH, then
    standard install locations). No personal paths remain in this package.
  - Added WINDOWS-PORT.md documenting the port.

  No upstream file was removed from the license/citation layer: LICENSE and
  CITATION.cff are preserved verbatim.

